                                "example_id": "cae9e080-4300-4b7a-a686-2c8ec77f7104",
                                "sense_id": "77fdd350-2d4b-3cfd-adf5-71784fde2bd1",
                                "text": "The A.D.A. figures utilized in this study include the claimables for state aid plus the nonclaimables."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1d9c9e12-4a58-4640-becf-f63362885c41",
                                "sense_id": "77fdd350-2d4b-3cfd-adf5-71784fde2bd1",
                                "text": "So, for example, if the conditional and negation introduced in terms of pragmatic incompatibility really are a conditional and negation — letting us say that two claimables are inferentially related as premise and conclusion, or that they are incompatible — then what those locutions work on must be genuine propositional contents — what appears embedded as the antecedent of the conditional, or is negated."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7da03a51-65f8-4cd5-b56f-378a748e1172",
                                "sense_id": "77fdd350-2d4b-3cfd-adf5-71784fde2bd1",
                                "text": "But it does not follow that there were no true claimables."
                            }
                        ]
